.TH "SKOGAI RUNNER-WO-RUN" 1  "skogai runner-wo-run 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
skogai runner\-wo\-run \- run a workorder, write <name>.result.json beside it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskogai runner wo run\fR [OPTIONS] <WORKORDER>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.br
run a workorder, write <name>.result.json beside it
.br

.br
with \-\-sandbox (or `sandbox: true` in the workorder) the worker runs in a
.br
fresh `skogai module sandbox` at .skogai/tmp/sandbox/<name>: its cwd is the
.br
sandbox repo, its skogai config is the sandbox's, every module found from
.br
here is installed there. the sandbox is kept for a look afterwards.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-model\fR=\fIMODEL\fR
.br
model, default the workorder's or runner.model
.TP
\fB\-\-sandbox\fR
.br
run the worker in a sandbox
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.br
Print help
.TP
<\fIWORKORDER\fR>
.br
name or path
